**How to implement.** The `.ocproj` file and its autosave sidewrite go: no window ever saved or opened one (001 §0, §R; .spec-md §7: '`.ocproj`, `recent.json`, autosave files — compatibility break accepted'). Kits replace them (S4.1–S4.3). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectFile.fs` (`ProjectFile.fs:ProjectFile`: `extension`, `FileName.saveProject`, `FileName.openProject`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:24`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs`: the `Autosave` module (`RecentFiles.fs:Autosave`: `autosaveSuffix`, `FileName.autosavePath`, `FileName.writeAutosave`) is deleted, with `open OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile`, `open OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project` and any other open left unused. `RecentFiles` keeps `maxRecent`, `prefsPath`, `bump`, `loadRecent` and `FileName.pushRecent` unchanged, as S5.1 replaces them. Its module doc (`RecentFiles.fs:11-17`) becomes one to three lines saying what stays: the most-recently-used list, kept in the per-user `recent.json` through the shared options; `loadRecent`'s doc (`:47`) says 'paths' for '`.ocproj` paths'. No comment in the file names autosave, `saveProject` or `.ocproj`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`: every comment that names `ProjectFile` or autosave (`:16-19`, `:25-27`, `:32-34`) is cut to the words that stay true; nothing is added (AGENTS.md). (4) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/ExperimentDataStore.fs` is in scope for its module doc only: a sentence of it that still names `FileName.openProject` or `ProjectFile.fs` as a precedent (`ExperimentDataStore.fs:19-20` today, in the doc step 135 rewrote) goes. (5) `.gitignore`: the `*.autosave` rule, its two-line comment and the blank line after them (`.gitignore:341-344`) are deleted. (6) Tests. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/RoundTripTests.fs` (`RoundTripTests.fs:RoundTripTests`, the `.ocproj` round trip and its load-time refusals) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`. What it proved holds for kit files in `KitContentFileJsonTests` (step 146): `an experiment file round-trips through its canonical text`, `an experiment file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed experiment file is refused before it binds`. In `HistoryTests.fs`, `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` (`HistoryTests.fs:90-110`) is deleted with the fixtures only it used (`filmThickness`, `vacuumSystem`, `light`, `node`, `projectWith`, `preEdit`, `edited`) and every open left unused (`OpticalConstructor.Domain.Project`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.ProjectFile`, `OpticalConstructor.Storage.Autosave` and the engine opens). The class keeps `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` with its assertions; only its paths change, written as kit folders, not `.ocproj` files: `C:\kits\a`, `C:\kits\b`, `C:\KITS\A` and `C:\kits\f<i>`, so the head is `C:\kits\f20` and the last `C:\kits\f5`. Its module doc becomes one line naming `RecentFiles.bump`'s most-recent-first rule. Afterwards `git grep -n -i -E "ProjectFile|autosave" -- Berreman/ .gitignore` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the project file and the autosave are deleted, `git grep -n -i -E "ProjectFile|autosave" -- Berreman/ .gitignore` MUST find nothing and `.gitignore` MUST hold no `*.autosave` rule; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` over kit-folder paths and every KitContentFileJsonTests fact, the count falling by 4; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.
